---
description: When a Tampermonkey userscript is updated, give the new script link and the links where existing installs must be pasted.
globs: docs/downloads/**/*.{txt,user.js}
alwaysApply: false
---

When a userscript version changes, end the reply with both of these. Do this every time, including when the files are already on main.

1. New script link. The raw URL of the `.user.js` that Tampermonkey installs, on `main` once that file is there:
   `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rigoabell/abelrigm_repository/main/docs/downloads/<file>.user.js`
   If it is not on `main` yet, give the branch raw URL that returns the file now, and say when the `main` link starts working.

2. Paste-in links. These are the places copies already installed still check. Name the page to open and the file to replace:
   - Productivity Panel: https://gist.github.com/rigoabell/60993861e496361e9d79fd5465de2973 — replace `MEM3-Productivity-Panel.user.js`
   - Peculiar Line Flush: https://github.com/rigoabell/peculiar-line-flush — replace `peculiar-line-flush.user.js` on `main`
   - Any other script: use the `@updateURL` that the previously published copy checks, even if this repository's copy now points somewhere else.

People on an older install do not see a new version until the file at their old update link is replaced. Say that when those paste-in links were not updated.
